menu "Station: receiver flasher"

    config UM98X_FLASH_ENABLE
        bool "Receiver firmware updates (send packages to the receiver)"
        default y
        help
            Builds the receiver flasher in: a receiver package the user
            confirmed (a release from the update banner, or an uploaded
            file) is sent to the receiver's loader, and an interrupted
            update is finished at boot. Off: packages can still be uploaded
            and checked against every pre-flight rule, the web UI says that
            receiver firmware updates are not enabled in this build, and
            nothing is ever sent to the receiver's loader. On in releases
            since v0.1.6, after updates on a UM980 (the NTRIP-X: 11833
            again, then 11833 to 23980). The UM982 uses the same loader
            steps; no UM982 update has run on hardware yet.

    config UM98X_FLASH_RECOVERY_ACTIONS
        bool "Send the boot-time recovery actions for an interrupted receiver update"
        depends on UM98X_FLASH_ENABLE
        default n
        help
            With an open receiver-flash journal, the boot picks the first
            bytes, baud rates and timeouts from the journal state and the
            reset reason (for example racing into the receiver's loader
            after a power cut). Off: it logs what it would send and sends
            nothing; the session then waits for the user. PROVISIONAL, to be
            confirmed on hardware.
            Not ready to turn on: the table takes a power-on reset for a
            receiver restart, but on the ESP32-S3 a reset by the EN pin
            (the USB serial chip's auto-reset, the RST button) reads as
            power-on while the receiver keeps running, still in its loader
            or in a transfer. The recovery must check the receiver first
            (station.c, station_early_boot).

    config UM98X_FLASH_FALLBACK_115200
        bool "Allow the 115200 baud fallback for loader entry and transfer"
        depends on UM98X_FLASH_ENABLE
        default n
        help
            Loader entry and transfer run at 460800. When enabled, an entry
            attempt that follows a failed attempt which never reached the
            loader prompt may run at 115200 instead. It is one of the
            session's three entry attempts, under the same journal: it never
            starts a second session on its own, and once the attempts are
            used up a new try needs the user's confirmation. Off until it is
            proven on hardware. PROVISIONAL, to be confirmed on hardware.

    config UM98X_FLASH_CROSS_LAYOUT
        bool "Allow packages with another partition layout (with their own confirmation)"
        depends on UM98X_FLASH_ENABLE
        default y
        help
            A package whose partition table differs from the one of the
            receiver's current build moves receiver flash regions. Refused
            while off; when on, such a package still needs its own explicit
            confirmation. Tested on hardware: a UM980 from build 11833 to
            23980 (the NTRIP-X, 2026-10-22). A UM982 layout change is not
            tested yet.

    config UM98X_FLASH_BYTE_CAPTURE
        bool "Capture every receiver byte (bench builds)"
        default n
        help
            Every byte sent to and received from the receiver by the
            flasher and the bench console, time-stamped as hex and text, in
            a 256 KB PSRAM ring (downloadable from the web UI's Logs > Console)
            and on the console. Selected by the bench console; never in a
            release.

endmenu
